  "id": "culture-shock",
  "term": "culture shock",
  "definition": "Culture shock is the stress and disorientation a person may feel when entering a new cultural environment, often beginning before arrival and becoming stronger in the first weeks or months. It can involve emotional and bodily signs such as anxiety, self-doubt, insecurity, irritability, poor concentration, tiredness, and a strong wish to return home.",
